WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.334
-My first guest tonight is

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.403
an Emmy- and
Golden Globe-winning actor.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.806
She directed and stars in
the new movie "Moxie,"

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.942
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.543
You have to watch it.
It is so good.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.478
Here is Amy Poehler!

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.680
Ah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.751
See? Ah, I missed you, buddy.
So good to see you.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:20.520
-Hi! Hi, Jimmy.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.155
-I want to get into "Moxie"

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.558
and what a great job
you did directing that.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.828
But it was so great to see you
hosting the Golden Globes.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.697
You were fantastic.
You were so funny.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:32.965
You looked great.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.868
But I know, from hosting
these awards shows,

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.303
it is a lot of work.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:41.740
I can't imagine what it was like
hosting one during a pandemic.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.042
-Yeah, you know what it's like.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.545
There's a lot of things
that can go wrong.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.513
And I had -- It was interesting,

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:49.749
'cause I had, like,
new stress dreams.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.917
You know, usually,
your dreams are that

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:54.254
you're going to, you know,
say the wrong thing

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.322
or you're gonna, you know, fall.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.692
But I kept having these, like,
technological stress dreams

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.794
that, you know,
was just going to disappear.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.128
Just like bloop!

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:05.631
-Like, bad edit-- Like,
the audio going out or something

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.067
or people cutting
to the wrong camera?

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.535
-Mm! All those.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.470
Like, basically like
a living Zoom nightmare

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.772
is what I was having.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.274
-But it was kind of --
It was like a Kubrick film,

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:20.512
because every -- The audience
was masked and quiet

00:01:20.512 --> 00:01:24.184
and spread out
and just kind of staring at us.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.651
-Wowsers.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.253
It's a lot, a lot,
a lot of work.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.787
And, man, I can't --

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:33.560
On behalf of everyone who saw
it, thank you so much.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.462
Like a lot of people
during this past year,

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.965
I've heard that
you've gotten into TikTok.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.367
Is that right?
-Yeah. Big-time.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.468
-Whoa!
-Big Tok.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.569
-Talk to me.
-Big-time.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:44.737
-Really?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.806
-Well, you know what
I do like about it a lot?

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:51.343
Is that I like that it takes
an idea, audio,

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:52.845
and it kind of --
You know, like,

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:56.215
people just decide how they're
going to deconstruct something.

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.817
And so I like that, you know,

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.319
a joke just keeps getting done

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.654
and then change into
something else

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.389
or the pastiche of it all.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.991
Someone takes someone's audio
and someone's video

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.025
and then comments.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:10.229
-It just, like --
It feels very D.I.Y.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:13.399
And then, speaking of
the Golden Globes,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.969
I saw La'Ron Hines,
the great, sweet La'Ron Hines,

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:20.406
who is, like, a TikTok star,
dare I say.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:24.410
And he interviews kids at his
mom's daycare in Mississippi.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.947
And we ended up having him
on the Golden Globes.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.148
-Isn't that cool?

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.251
That's amazing that you --
I loved that part.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.152
That was great. That's wild.
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.855
-I did --
I'm doing more TikToks.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.756
But I did my first one,

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:40.293
and I want to say it
took me like three hours to do.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.661
I go...

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.963
-Yeah, I don't do any.
I don't do any.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.832
I don't.
I don't add any value to TikTok.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:50.102
I just watch it and go,
"Good for him.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.370
She's right."
-Right?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.005
That's good.
You got to love it.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.575
-I'm like, "Oh, that's what
that button does."

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.676
Stuff like that.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.644
That's what TikTok
helps me with.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:02.014
"Oh, that's how
I can clean my sink."

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yeah! That's what I --
Dude, I love the hacks.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.587
-Show me a better way
to fold my chip bag,

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:09.822
and you got me for life.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.657
-Dude, what's this thing
about frying cheese?

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:15.528
I never knew that you -- If you
fry cheese, like, really thin,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:19.132
you can use that as kind of
like the bread almost.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.300
-Oh, boy, that's gonna --
-No, it's insane.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.601
I've already --
I was just watching it.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.905
-What if I just --
I immediately ran out of frame,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:30.276
and you started -- You heard the
sizzling sound of cheese.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:36.115
-Look, I know you as a great
comedian, a writer, an actor.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.984
And I know you directed,

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:41.654
but now you directed
your second movie, "Moxie."

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.390
It is on Netflix now.
It is fantastic.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.092
And I just want to say
I love it,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.927
because I have two girls now.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:51.264
And I don't know -- I'm also a
coming-of-age-movie fan.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.331
But I don't know if
there is a movie

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.066
that's kind of like this movie,

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:56.602
that's for girls, where --
It's for everybody,

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.805
I mean, but I feel like
there's nothing out there

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.740
for my girls to watch
where they go like,

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.508
"Oh, yeah,
that's an awesome message."

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:05.545
That is so cool.
I just loved it.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.446
I thought it was well-done,
top to bottom.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:08.680
-Thank you very much.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.950
I mean, we grew up
with the same movies, right?

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:15.287
So, I always loved those
high-school movies that had,

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:17.857
you know, kind of
the quiet female protagonist,

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.459
like Molly Ringwald,
if you will,

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.828
who was watching the action

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.763
and trying to figure out
how to participate in it.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.832
And, you know, the book that it
was based on is, you know,

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.335
written by
a high-school teacher.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.070
And we really wanted it
to feel like

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.406
what high school feels like --
high stakes, big feelings.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:35.908
-It really is high stakes.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.043
I mean, when you're --

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.144
especially when
you're in high school.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.279
It's like, you don't --
Now we're older,

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.215
I don't think about that,
but you're like,

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.483
"Oh, no, no, this is
the biggest thing in the world."

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:45.584
-Oh, big-time.

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:48.187
I mean I have a feeling
you and I

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.122
had very similar
high-school experiences.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.423
I mean, I don't know about you,

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:53.960
but I had a big high school,
lots of different groups.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.228
-Yeah.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:58.931
-You really had to kind of
declare who you were.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:04:59.999
There was a lot of lists.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.934
Like, a lot of superlatives --

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.636
like,
inappropriate superlatives.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.638
-Yeah, I'm trying to think of
what I can even say anymore.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.273
But yeah.
-I know, you can't.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:09.308
Like, I know we had, like,
Class Flirt

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:12.377
and Best Couple
and Best Eyes and Cutest.

00:05:12.377 --> 00:05:15.114
And it was like, "God!

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.984
Why don't you just put Nice Rack
on there and call it a day."

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:21.120
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.955
-That's what I won!

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.824
-You got Nice Rack?!
-Yeah, in high school.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:25.991
That was me.
-Congratulations!

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.226
-Thank you. I was excited.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.360
I'll take what
I can get, though.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.130
-You had a really nice rack
on your car,

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.399
on the top of your car?

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.500
-Like, horns and stuff.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.968
It wasn't real animal,
of course.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.705
-Yeah, it was a nice rack.
It should win.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:42.508
-Can you tell everyone
what "Moxie" is about?

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:46.311
-Sure. So, it's -- "Moxie"
is about a 16-year-old girl

00:05:46.311 --> 00:05:50.416
who is trying to figure out how
she fits into her high school.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:55.488
She has a mom who is a more
extroverted, rebel-girl past.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:06:00.092
And she doesn't know how
to speak up

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:03.896
and speak out against the things
that are bothering her

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.698
and that are dangerous
in her school.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:10.403
So she gets inspired by a zine
and she makes one

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.037
and she leaves it in her school.

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:15.608
And it's taken over by
the other women in the school.

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:19.378
And together, they try to
bring the system down.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:20.846
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:23.449
Here's Amy Poehler in
her new movie, "Moxie."

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.883
Take a look at this.

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:26.985
-Me and my friends,
we protested everything.

00:06:26.985 --> 00:06:29.655
One time, someone told
our friend Sarah

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:32.358
that she smelled, and none of us
showered for two weeks.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.459
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:34.794
Yeah.

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.828
-But how do you know what to do,

00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:38.931
like, how to protest something?

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.032
-We didn't.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.034
You know,
we made a ton of mistakes.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:43.202
We argued with each other.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.171
We weren't
intersectional enough.

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:47.105
We called our meetings pow-wows.

00:06:47.105 --> 00:06:49.742
-Oh, no.
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.611
-But you're glad
you did it all, right?

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:52.778
-Of course.

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:54.380
What are you going to do?
Nothing?

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.681
-Amy Poehler, everybody!

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.950
"Moxie" is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.351
By the way, congrats on it being

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:01.520
the number-1 movie
on Netflix, bud.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.922
That's the way to do it.
-How cool?

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.191
-That is the way to do it,
Amy Poehler!

